ken by lightest bodyweight."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "With the new heavyweight class added internationally in 1969, the unlimited class was now for lifters weight 110 kg or more, as the lifters were getting bigger and bigger. Soviet " [:a {:href ""} "Leonid Zhabotinsky"] " had won this division in 1964-68 but was now retired. His successor was " [:a {:href "/athletes/56889"} "Vasily Alekseyev"] ", who won the 1970 and 1971 World Championships. His biggest challengers were considered to be Belgian " [:a {:href "/athletes/55253"} "Serge Reding"] ", the 1968 silver medalist and 1969 World Champion, and American " [:a {:href "/athletes/57011"} "Ken Patera"] ", runner-up to Alekseyev at the 1971 Worlds. Reding failed to make a valid lift in the press, and Patera met the same fate in the snatch, leaving Alekseyev with no competition. He won the gold medal with a 30 kg margin over West German " [:a {:href "/athletes/55844"} "Rudolf Mang"] ", with East German " [:a {:href "/athletes/55787"} "Gerd Bonk"] " in third place. Alekseyev would return at Montréal in 1976 and defend the gold medal. He tried to win a third gold medal in 1980, but missed his three snatch attempts in Moskva."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Kilograms"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/56889"} "Vasily Alekseyev"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/URS.png"}] "URS"]] [:td {} "640.0"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "Olympic Record"} "OR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/55844"} "Rudolf Mang"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRG"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: